// Closing a file descriptor, which only a Linux kernel hands the backend: the
// dma-buf an exported texture's memory is. The call is made to the kernel
// directly, so this file takes part only in a build for a platform with that
// kernel behind it (KLF section 27.8), and `closeDescriptor!` reaches it there.

import Foundation on linux, tessera

@FFI.Syscall { name: close }
function vulkanCloseDescriptor(descriptor: Int) -> Int
